WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.099
Gradient just means “how fast”.

2
00:00:01.099 --> 00:00:04.778
How fast one thing changes when another thing changes.

3
00:00:04.778 --> 00:00:08.175
On a straight line, gradient = rise ÷ run.

4
00:00:08.175 --> 00:00:11.571
120 km in 2 hours: 120 ÷ 2 = 60 km per hour.

5
00:00:11.571 --> 00:00:14.967
On a curve the gradient keeps changing.

6
00:00:14.967 --> 00:00:18.363
The tangent at a point gives the gradient right there.

7
00:00:18.363 --> 00:00:21.759
Differentiate to get the gradient anywhere: y = x² gives dy/dx = 2x.

8
00:00:21.759 --> 00:00:25.156
At x = 3 the gradient is 2 × 3 = 6.

9
00:00:25.156 --> 00:00:29.684
Where dy/dx = 0 the tangent is flat: a maximum or a minimum.

10
00:00:29.684 --> 00:00:34.242
Give the gradient with its units, like metres per second.

11
00:00:34.212 --> 00:00:39.241
